Subject: [PATCH] linux-atm: make declarations consistent and cover vt_id

p_factory.c defined send_cache_imposition_reply's last parameter as
uint8_t cli_atm_addr[ATM_ESA_LEN] while packets.h:42 declares it uint8_t *.
The two are compatible in C (an array parameter decays), but gcc's
-Warray-parameter flags the mismatched bound. Match the header.

qgen's copy_block() switches on VALUE_TYPE, which has four members
(qgen.h:9: vt_id, vt_case, vt_multi, vt_length), but only handled three.
vt_id owns no pointers - VALUE.id is an interned const char* - so the shallow
struct copy performed just above the switch is already complete. Add an
explicit `case vt_id: break;` to say so rather than leaving -Wswitch to guess.

ql_y.c is shipped in the tarball alongside ql_y.y and automake's .y.c rule is
guarded by am__skipyacc, so patch both to stay correct either way.

--- a/src/mpoad/p_factory.c
+++ b/src/mpoad/p_factory.c
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@
 				uint8_t  code,
 				uint8_t  prefix_length,
 				uint16_t mtu,
-				uint8_t  cli_atm_addr[ATM_ESA_LEN]
+				uint8_t *cli_atm_addr
 				){
   int pos = 0;
   struct nhrp_fixed_h *fixed;
--- a/src/qgen/ql_y.c
+++ b/src/qgen/ql_y.c
@@ -166,6 +166,8 @@
 	    (*new_field)->value = alloc_t(VALUE);
 	    *(*new_field)->value = *orig_field->value;
 	    switch (orig_field->value->type) {
+		case vt_id:
+		    break;
 		case vt_length:
 		    (*new_field)->value->block =
 		      copy_block(orig_field->value->block);
--- a/src/qgen/ql_y.y
+++ b/src/qgen/ql_y.y
@@ -96,6 +96,8 @@
 	    (*new_field)->value = alloc_t(VALUE);
 	    *(*new_field)->value = *orig_field->value;
 	    switch (orig_field->value->type) {
+		case vt_id:
+		    break;
 		case vt_length:
 		    (*new_field)->value->block =
 		      copy_block(orig_field->value->block);
